        "username": "ana.lima",
        "display_name": "Ana Lima"
      },
      "content": "Yes. Either copy it (`let first = v[0];`, since `i32` is `Copy`) or finish using the reference before you push:\n\n```rust\nlet mut v = vec![1, 2, 3];\nlet first = v[0];\nv.push(4);\nprintln!(\"{first}\");\n```\n\nThe [book chapter on references](https://doc.rust-lang.org/book/ch04-02-references-and-borrowing.html) walks through the same example.",
      "created_at": "2026-10-12T18:40:00Z",
      "edited_at": "2026-10-12T18:52:00Z",
      "is_solution": true
    },
